{
  "id": "28561_dakoku",
  "headword": "{打刻|だこく}",
  "reading": "だこく",
  "romaji": "dakoku",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "clocking in/out; stamping the time",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "clocking in/out; stamping the time on a record",
      "explanation": "The act of recording one's start or end of work time, traditionally by stamping a time card and now often by scanning a card or using a smartphone app."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "28561_dakoku_ex1",
      "japanese": "{出社|しゅっしゃ}したら{打刻|だこく}してください。",
      "english": "Please clock in when you arrive at the office.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28561_dakoku_ex2",
      "japanese": "{昨日|きのう}は{退勤|たいきん}の{打刻|だこく}を{忘|わす}れてしまった。",
      "english": "Yesterday I forgot to clock out.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28561_dakoku_ex3",
      "japanese": "{当社|とうしゃ}ではICカードを{使|つか}って{出退勤|しゅったいきん}の{打刻|だこく}を{行|おこな}っています。",
      "english": "At our company, we use IC cards to record clock-in and clock-out times.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Literally 'stamp engraving'. Originally referred to the act of physically stamping a time card; now used broadly for any electronic time-recording action. Common in workplace HR documents.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {打刻|だこく}する: to clock in/out\n- {出勤|しゅっきん}の{打刻|だこく}: clock-in (recording)\n- {退勤|たいきん}の{打刻|だこく}: clock-out (recording)\n- {打刻|だこく}{漏|も}れ: missed clock-in/out\n- {打刻|だこく}{時刻|じこく}: time recorded\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- タイムカード: time card\n- {勤怠|きんたい}{管理|かんり}: attendance management\n- {打刻|だこく}{機|き}: time clock machine",
